    "long_instructions": "# Revisiting the Final Project\r\n\r\n## Multi-Page Web Application\r\n\r\n#### In this unit’s final project, students take on the role of web designers to create a multi-page digital magazine for a fictional user or community.\r\n\r\n#### Across the unit, students build toward this project by practicing the same tools and design strategies they will apply in their final work. They develop ideas through iteration, refining layouts and content with a focus on how real users will experience the site.\r\n\r\n#### Students define a target audience and brand identity, plan key pages such as the home and article pages, and use AI in Guide Mode to generate the HTML and CSS that bring their designs to life.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/0fa53a5cbf5480e4c10f9f2bc406506f-image-1765910932701.png\" alt=\"Sample student project of a website giving informaiton about events happening locally in their community\" width=\"850px\" style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\r\n\r\n## You Did It! \r\n\r\n#### You’ve now explored the tools, concepts, and workflows students will use to complete this project. This module is designed to give you a clear picture of how the unit builds toward the final outcome and to help you feel prepared to guide students through the process.\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 18px; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;\">\r\n    ➡️ <strong>Optional: </strong>Open the <a href='https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-semester2-2025/units/1/lessons/13' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>Project Lesson Plan</a> to review when you're done with this module.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n## Reflection\r\n\r\n>#### Name one concept from earlier in the module that students will draw on during the final project, and explain how you expect them to do so.\r\n\r\n<div style=\"display: flex; align-items: left; margin:20px 0px 30px 0px\">\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://forum.code.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/7dbe63a051fbad4ef262d6ab710e2966-image-1731959037460.png\" style=\"width: auto; height: 100px;\"  alt=\"A browser with two text boxes, both including an avatar and lines of text.\"></a>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #007786; border-radius: 20px 20px 20px 20px; color: #000000; width: 80%; margin-left: 5%; margin-right: 5%; padding: 10px 10px 5px 10px;\">\r\n\r\n<p style=\"color: white; line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; font-size: 18px\"><b>Post to the Code.org Forum</b></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"color: white; line-height: 1.2; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; font-size: 18px\">Share your response and read other educators' ideas on the forum! Click on the icon to the left to direct to our forum post.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n",
